```c
if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    ...
} else {
    ...
}
```
Reason:
The code incorrectly checks for active elements in all cases when re-inserting an inactive element into the red-black tree. This leads to an infinite loop because it does not select a next branch to inspect when the element is inactive, causing the insertion process to hang indefinitely.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (nft_rbtree_interval_end(rbe) &&
    !nft_rbtree_interval_end(new)) {
    p = &parent->rb_left;
} else if (!nft_rbtree_interval_end(rbe) &&
           nft_rbtree_interval_end(new)) {
    p = &parent->rb_right;
} else if (nft_set_elem_active(&rbe->ext, genmask)) {
    *ext = &rbe->ext;
    return -EEXIST;
}
```
Reason:
The patch restricts the check for active elements to only the EEXIST case, allowing the code to properly handle the re-insertion of inactive elements without entering an infinite loop. This ensures that the next branch is selected correctly based on the interval conditions, preventing the endless loop during the insertion process.

